# Inject a WallClock capability

When code must observe time more than once or schedule work, depend on `WallClock` from `@enormora/wall-clock`. Prefer subpaths `@enormora/wall-clock/wall-clock` and `@enormora/wall-clock/deterministic-wall-clock`. The clock exposes `currentTimestampInMilliseconds`, `currentDate`, `setTimeout`, `clearTimeout`, `setInterval`, and `clearInterval`.

Production calls `createWallClock()` at the composition root. Tests call `createDeterministicWallClock({ initialCurrentTimestampInMilliseconds })` and move time with `advanceByMilliseconds` or `setCurrentTimestampInMilliseconds`. Do not use Mocha or Sinon fake timers.

This package is not a date-fns replacement. It only makes observation and scheduling explicit. Use it for wall-clock time, not monotonic performance measurement.

```typescript
import assert from 'node:assert';
import { createDeterministicWallClock } from '@enormora/wall-clock/deterministic-wall-clock';
import { createWallClock, type WallClock } from '@enormora/wall-clock/wall-clock';

// ❌ Orchestration calls globals. Tests would patch setTimeout.
function scheduleRefresh(refreshAt: number, refresh: () => void): void {
    setTimeout(refresh, refreshAt - Date.now());
}

// ✅ Same factory in production and tests. Tests own the timeline.
function createScheduleRefresh(wallClock: WallClock) {
    return function scheduleRefresh(refreshAt: number, refresh: () => void) {
        const delay = Math.max(0, refreshAt - wallClock.currentTimestampInMilliseconds);
        return wallClock.setTimeout(refresh, delay);
    };
}

createScheduleRefresh(createWallClock());

suite('scheduleRefresh', function () {
    test('runs at the scheduled timestamp', function () {
        const wallClock = createDeterministicWallClock({
            initialCurrentTimestampInMilliseconds: 1_704_067_200_000
        });
        let ran = 0;
        createScheduleRefresh(wallClock)(1_704_067_205_000, function () {
            ran += 1;
        });
        wallClock.advanceByMilliseconds(4_999);
        assert.strictEqual(ran, 0);
        wallClock.advanceByMilliseconds(1);
        assert.strictEqual(ran, 1);
    });
});
```
